# Architecture rules

## Bounded contexts

- `shop` and `trustpay` never share tables, domain types (except `src/contracts/trustpay.ts`), or imports.
- Shop code (`app/(shop)`, `app/(merchant)`, `app/api/shop`, `modules/shop`, shop/merchant components) may import `lib/trustpay-client` and `contracts/trustpay` only. Never import `modules/trustpay` or use Prisma models prefixed `Tp`.
- TrustPay code (`modules/trustpay`, `app/trustpay`, `app/api/trustpay`, trustpay components) may import `contracts/trustpay` only from the shared layer. Never import `modules/shop` or shop models.
- `contracts/` imports only `zod`.

## Ports and adapters

- External capabilities are interfaces (`MobileMoneyProvider`, `Clock`, `WebhookTransport`) with simulated implementations injected via `createTrustPayContext()`.
- Business logic must not call telecom APIs or raw `fetch` for MoMo; go through ports.

## Domain invariants

- Status changes go through transition tables (state machines), never ad hoc if-chains. Illegal transitions return `409 invalid_transition`.
- Ledger is the source of truth: balances derived from immutable double-entry rows.
- A state change, its ledger entries, and its outbox event are written in ONE DB transaction.
- Mutating APIs, webhooks, and cron jobs are idempotent.
- Money is integers in pesewas (`*Minor`), currency `GHS`, never floats.
- Time in TrustPay comes from the `Clock` port (demo offset via `TpDemoClock`).

## Fail closed

- Validate all inputs with zod at every boundary; reject unknown fields.
- Authorization checked server-side on every route (not only middleware).
